---
/**
 * Playing: what a DJ needs at the mixer, in the order they need it. The reason in three sentences,
 * the drawing of the meters, the three lines to know by heart, then the two procedures and whose
 * controls are whose. Each instruction is said once, where it is used.
 *
 * The drawing comes before the lines because they name its lights: "first orange" and "top orange"
 * mean nothing until the reader has seen which lights they are. Nothing here is for the crew:
 * MASTER ATT, UTILITY and the amps are on Crew.
 */
import KnowByHeart from '../components/KnowByHeart.astro';
import LegacyAnchors from '../components/LegacyAnchors.astro';
import MeterTargets from '../components/MeterTargets.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Procedure from '../components/Procedure.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ZERO_MARK } from '../lib/checklists';
import { GLOSSARY } from '../lib/glossary';
import { DJ_RULES } from '../lib/rules';
import { GUIDE, section } from '../lib/sections';
import { href } from '../lib/url';

const moved = Object.fromEntries([
  ...GUIDE.filter((p) => p.id !== 'playing').flatMap((p) => [p.id, ...p.sections.map((s) => s.id)]),
  'check', 'myths', 'reference', 'glossary', 'sources', 'model', 'record-level', 'loud',
  ...Object.keys(GLOSSARY).map((key) => `word-${key}`),
  ...['headroom', 'louder', 'limiter', 'videos', 'quiet-file', 'digital'].map((id) => `myth-${id}`),
].map((id) => [id, `/learn/#${id === 'loud' ? 'myths' : id}`]));
---

<Base title="Out of the red: keep your set’s recording clean" description="Every set here is recorded, straight from the mixer. Where to aim on the meters, how to set TRIM for each track, and what to do when a blend reads high.">
  <PageHeader title="Playing a set" lede="Every set here is recorded, straight from the mixer.">
    <p>No limiter sits between the mixer and the recorder. If the mixer clips, the crunch is in the recording. If you turn the recording down, the crunch gets quieter. It does not go away.</p>
  </PageHeader>
  <div class="flow page-body" id="playing">
    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="meters">
      <h2 id="meters">{section('meters').title}</h2>
      <MeterTargets />
    </section>

    <KnowByHeart title="When you’re playing" rules={DJ_RULES} refs={false} />

    <div class="page-group section-start">
      <Procedure id="trim" title="Set TRIM in your headphones" level={2} kind="Every track" steps={[
        { challenge: 'Channel fader', response: 'down' },
        { challenge: 'TRIM, HI, MID and LOW', response: '12 o’clock' },
        { challenge: 'Track', response: 'in your headphones, loudest part playing' },
        { challenge: 'TRIM', response: 'channel meter on the first orange (0)', note: ZERO_MARK },
        { challenge: 'Channel fader', response: 'up, when you mix it in' },
      ]}>
        <p>Tracks arrive at different levels, and the knob’s position does not tell you the level. A lower setting is fine: a clean recording can be turned up afterwards.</p>
        <details><summary>Why this target</summary><p>The XDJ-RX2 manual asks for orange at a track’s loudest part and warns against red (p.&nbsp;31). For the MASTER meters it names a level: around 0&nbsp;dB at the peak (p.&nbsp;34). The first orange is that 0, and it leaves room for a blend. <a href={href('/learn/#red-top')}>Read the evidence and limits</a>.</p></details>
      </Procedure>

      <Procedure id="blends" title="MASTER meters: top orange lit" level={2} kind="In a blend" steps={[
        { challenge: 'A channel fader', response: 'down a little', note: 'Use the incoming track’s fader. If both are already up, either one works.' },
        { challenge: 'HI, MID and LOW', response: '12 o’clock or lower', note: 'Boosting EQ adds level too.' },
        { challenge: 'MASTER meters', response: 'top orange dark again' },
      ]}>
        <p>Two tracks add together, by up to two lights. If CLIP blinks, even slowly, do the same at once. <a href={href('/learn/#blends')}>Try a blend and see the meters change</a>.</p>
      </Procedure>
    </div>

    <section class="page-section section-start" aria-labelledby="knobs">
      <h2 id="knobs">{section('knobs').title}</h2>
      <dl class="deflist">
        <div>
          <dt id="yours">Yours</dt>
          <dd>TRIM (the top knob on each channel), HI, MID and LOW, the channel faders, BOOTH MONITOR (top right) and HEADPHONES LEVEL (bottom left).</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt id="crews">The crew’s</dt>
          <dd>MASTER LEVEL (top centre, above the meters). It sets the room and the recording together. For a louder room, ask the crew: they turn up the amps, and the recording stays as it is.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <p><a href={href('/learn/')}>Learn why and practise</a>, with listening tests and a blend to try.</p>
    <LegacyAnchors map={moved} />
  </div>
</Base>
